Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.11,0:00:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Every drop of rain that falls on land begins
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.03,0:00:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,a slow journey back to the sea
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.58,0:00:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,As rainwater runs over rocks and through soil
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.07,0:00:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,it dissolves tiny amounts of minerals mostly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.01,0:00:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,sodium and chloride
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.92,0:00:17.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Rivers carry those minerals downstream mile
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.12,0:00:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,after mile until they reach the ocean
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:23.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The rivers themselves taste fresh because the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.12,0:00:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,amount of salt in any single drop is almost
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.42,0:00:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,nothing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.29,0:00:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But the ocean has been collecting those drops
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.57,0:00:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,for billions of years
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.42,0:00:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Water leaves the sea by evaporation
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.19,0:00:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It rises as vapor forms clouds and falls again
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.07,0:00:39.12,Default,,0,0,0,,as rain
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.12,0:00:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The salt cannot evaporate so it stays behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.51,0:00:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Deep on the ocean floor volcanic vents add
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.88,0:00:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,even more minerals pumping hot mineral-rich
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.38,0:00:51.14,Default,,0,0,0,,water into the dark
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.14,0:00:53.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Over time the balance settled
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.44,0:00:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Today seawater is about three and a half percent
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.39,0:00:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,salt
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.26,0:00:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,If you spread all of it across the land it
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.81,0:01:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,would form a layer more than one hundred meters
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.28,0:01:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,thick
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.21,0:01:06.12,Default,,0,0,0,,So the ocean is salty for a simple reason
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.12,0:01:09.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything flows into it and only the water
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.26,0:01:10.08,Default,,0,0,0,,ever leaves
